.TH VC4FAST 1 "2026-11-20" "vc4-stack" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vc4fast \- switch vc4d between the safe defaults and the speed-tuned drop-in
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vc4fast
[\fBon\fR|\fBoff\fR|\fBstatus\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vc4fast on
installs
.I /etc/systemd/system/vc4d.service.d/10-fast.conf
and restarts vc4d with the tuned recipe: arena 150 MiB and a 60 s launch
timeout.  These are the values measured for the 320x320 YOLOv8n graph.  The
reason for the larger arena is the graph's activations, weights and per-conv
im2col scratch; the reason for the longer timeout is the first run of a large
graph while the kernel cache is cold.
.PP
.B vc4fast off
removes the drop-in and restarts vc4d with the defaults from
.IR /etc/default/vc4d
(arena 96 MiB, 10 s).
.PP
.B vc4fast status
prints which configuration is active and the running daemon's argv.
.PP
No clock, governor or voltage is changed by any of these: the board stays at
stock core 400 MHz / V3D 300 MHz.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/vc4d.service.d/10-fast.conf
The drop-in, present when fast mode is on.
.TP
.I /etc/vc4/vc4d-fast.default
The tuned
.B VC4D_ARGS
selected by the drop-in.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vc4-query (1),
.BR vc4-smi (1),
.BR vc4d (8)
